  "note": "Two bands, both conditional on playing. tier: empirical quantiles of actual / projected (players who played) by position and projection tier, each position shrunk toward the pooled tier shape by n / (n + 40); a band is the projection \u00d7 these ratios. simulation: the player's own outcome distribution from his projected stat line \u2014 volume lognormal around its projection (volumeSigma), receptions binomial at his catch rate, yards = volume \u00d7 per-opportunity yardage lognormal (yardsPerOppSigma), TDs Poisson at his rate per opportunity (negative binomial where tdDispersion > 1), INTs Poisson \u2014 each draw scored; a TD-dependent or low-volume line gets a wider band. Published band = the average of the two quantile sets (simulation.coverage.blend checks it). The median sits below the projection because weeks are right-skewed. coverage = share of last week's actuals inside the bands fitted on the weeks before it (80% band should read ~0.80, 50% band ~0.50).",
